--- ASSESSMENT.txt ---
ENTRE PALAVRAS — delivery notes

Open universe/index.html directly in a browser. No server, build, or data fetch is needed. Example: universe/index.html?word=saudade

The initial view shows every canonical word and every distinct relation. Search is case- and accent-insensitive. Select a node or a neighbor button to see direct connections; drag to pan, scroll or use buttons to zoom, and use the home button to reset. The link button copies the current word URL where clipboard permission is available.

Extraction assumptions:
Only links in sections sinonimos and analogas describe lexical relations. Header, sidebar, footer, and index links are navigation. Redirect pages are aliases, resolved before collecting links. Canonical labels come from h1, lowercase and Unicode NFC, preserving accents. Missing targets are excluded rather than invented. A relation is an undirected pair; repeated links and self-links are removed. Isolated canonical entries would still be retained.

Findings: 256 HTML files, 250 word pages, 3 redirect aliases, 7 unresolved relation links. 250 words and 743 distinct pairs. Palavra and tempo tie at 16 neighbors. result.json uses the alphabetically first tied word for most_connected and records the complete tie in most_connected_ties.

Validation: verify.py checks graph symmetry, duplicate neighbors, missing endpoints, self-links, exact saudade neighbors, counts, and equality between embedded page data and words.json. browser-check.cjs executes the page JavaScript with a simulated DOM/canvas to check startup, deep linking, selection, reset, accent-insensitive search, and no-results state. JavaScript also passed node --check. These checks do not constitute a visual browser screenshot test. extraction-report.json records unresolved links and extraction details.

The page uses Canvas 2D with a deterministic force layout. Positions are an exploratory arrangement, not a semantic distance measurement. Colors are original site themes; larger nodes have more neighbors. Google Fonts is optional; system fonts work offline. No other external requests are required.


